Upstream-Name: photocraft
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/issues
Source: https://github.com/storytold/photocraft
Comment: The Rust crates that are linked into the programs are not listed here. gen-crate-licenses.py appends a
 paragraph for each of them (and the license paragraphs they need) when the package is built, and the build
 installs their license files under /usr/share/doc/storytold-photocraft*/vendor-licenses/. Upstream's NOTICE
 (installed as /usr/share/doc/storytold-photocraft*/NOTICE) lists the other third-party material that PhotoCraft bundles.

Files: *
Copyright: 2026, ArtCraft Team and the PhotoCraft contributors
License: Expat or Apache-2.0
Comment: upstream's NOTICE: "Licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License, Version 2.0, at your option".
 The ArtCraft name, wordmark and logos (docs/brand/) are trademarks and are not covered by that license; upstream
 describes their terms in docs/brand/LICENSE-brand.txt. This package does not install them (the programs do not
 refer to them). The application icon (assets/app-icon/) is not one of them: its own LICENSE.txt says it is
 original artwork, licensed under the Apache License 2.0 or the MIT license, at your option.

